---
source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: "help_of(&format!(\"{line} -h\"))"
---
Work with the objects on a board.

USAGE
  holst object <command> [flags]

COMMANDS
  ls:          List the objects of a board or a part of it
  add:         Add stickers, texts, shapes, frames, arrows, links, images, files, dice, a spinner wheel, sticker stacks, flip cards, mind-map nodes, documents, text stamps, code blocks, tables, reaction stamps, icons, task cards, kanbans or freehand strokes to a board
  edit:        Change text, corner, size, color, order or tags of objects
  cp:          Copy objects on their board or onto another board
  group:       Put objects into a group
  ungroup:     Dissolve groups; their objects stay
  lock:        Lock objects so that they cannot be changed
  unlock:      Unlock locked groups, frames and tables
  align:       Align objects to a side or spread them evenly
  rm:          Remove objects with what a frame holds and their arrows
  get:         Download the original of an image or file object

FLAGS
  -w, --workspace ws   Where a board name is looked up

ARGUMENTS
  The board is given as in `holst b -h`. Objects are given with --object: an id, a link,
  an @N from a listing, or the first 8 characters of the id; a link to an object
  as the board names that object too.

EXAMPLES
  $ holst o ls "Roadmap" -k sticker --contains "design"
  $ holst o add sticker "Roadmap" "Ask design" -c yellow4
  $ holst o add frame "Roadmap" "Q4" --items q4.json
  $ holst o rm "https://app.holst.so/board/…?object=…"
